module flsd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Southern District's own criminal periods. A criminal motion follows
// Local Rule 7.1 except 7.1(a)(3) and 7.1(b), carries a certificate of
// conferral, and a motion needing evidentiary support a concise statement
// of the material facts (88.9(a), (b)); proposed jury instructions name
// their source (88.9(d)). Retained counsel's fees are not good cause to
// withdraw after arraignment, and appearances state whether counsel is
// retained for trial only or for trial and appeal (88.7(a), (b)): no
// period. A defendant's request for the Standing Discovery Order is a
// FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(A)-(F) request, and the government's Brady, Giglio and
// other duties run under that order (88.10(a)-(n)). Discovery for a
// pre-trial hearing other than a bail or detention hearing is made at least
// forty-eight hours before it, and for a bail or detention hearing by its
// start (88.10(o)(1)); the language has no hour unit, so the 48 hours stay
// in this note, as do the duty magistrate judge's review of a criminal
// complaint within the earlier of forty-eight hours after arrest or the
// initial appearance (88.11). The conference "no later than fourteen (14)
// days after a defendant's arraignment" (88.10(o)(6)) is FRCrimP 16.1(a)'s
// own period and stays with lit/frcrimp. Petty offenses and collateral
// forfeiture (88.3) and appointed counsel under the CJA plan (88.1) state
// no period. The earlier outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions belong to
// lit/frcrimp and are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// The defendant's arraignment (S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.5, 88.9(c), 88.10(o)).
event Arraigned()
/// A party's written request for expert disclosure under FRCrimP
/// 16(a)(1)(G)(i) or 16(b)(1)(C)(i) (S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(3)(A)).
event ExpertSummaryRequested()
/// The date set for the commencement of trial (S.D. Fla. L.R.
/// 88.10(o)(3)(B)).
event TrialScheduled()
/// A guilty plea or a guilty verdict is entered (S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(a)).
event GuiltEntered()
/// The date set for the sentencing hearing (S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(b)).
event SentencingHearingScheduled()
/// The date set for a post-trial hearing, a sentencing hearing included
/// (S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(4)).
event PostTrialHearingScheduled()

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.5: within twenty-one days after arraignment, and
/// every twenty-one days after that until trial or a plea, counsel for the
/// government and each defendant file and serve a speedy trial status
/// report (agreed and disputed excludable time, and the last day for trial
/// under the court's Speedy Trial Plan). Only the first report is counted
/// here; each later one falls twenty-one days after the one before.
deadline speedy-trial-report-period: 21.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.5"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.9(c): motions in criminal cases are filed and served
/// within twenty-eight days from the arraignment of the defendant to whom
/// the motion applies; a motion arising from a post-arraignment event
/// within a reasonable time after the event.
deadline criminal-motion-period: 28.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.9(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(2): discovery in connection with trial is made
/// not later than fourteen days after the arraignment, or at another time
/// the court orders.
deadline trial-discovery-period: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(3)(A): the initial written summary of expert
/// testimony is provided within fourteen days of the written request, but
/// need not be provided earlier than fourteen days after the arraignment.
deadline expert-summary-period: 14.days after ExpertSummaryRequested() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(3)(B)(i), (iii): the full FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(G)
/// or 16(b)(1)(C) disclosure for testimony in a party's case-in-chief
/// (the defendant's mental-condition testimony included) is made no later
/// than twenty-one days before trial, but need not be made earlier than
/// fourteen days after the arraignment.
deadline expert-case-in-chief-disclosure-period: 21.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(3)(B)(ii), (iv): the disclosure for expert
/// testimony offered to counter the other side's timely disclosed expert
/// testimony is made no later than seven days before trial.
deadline expert-rebuttal-disclosure-period: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)(4): discovery in connection with a post-trial
/// hearing, a sentencing hearing included, is made not later than seven
/// days before the hearing (the presentence report follows 88.8).
deadline post-trial-discovery-period: 7.days before PostTrialHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.10(o)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(a): within seven days after a guilty plea or
/// verdict, defense counsel and the probation officer arrange the initial
/// presentence interview.
deadline presentence-interview-period: 7.days after GuiltEntered() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(b): counsel confer no later than seven days before
/// the sentencing hearing on its anticipated length and the number of
/// witnesses.
deadline sentencing-conference-period: 7.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(b): a party anticipating a sentencing proceeding
/// over one hour files and serves a notice of the witnesses and time
/// needed, with a courtesy copy to Probation, no later than five days
/// before it; any notice for enhancement of sentence or request for
/// departure is filed in the same period.
deadline sentencing-notice-period: 5.days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Fla. L.R. 88.8(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
